.SH NAME
anpu-doctor - Check the ANPU environment and data locations


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBanpu doctor [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Print ANPU's runtime environment: Go build info, the scan-history
DB path, whether Nuclei is installed (and its version), and whether the
report output directory is writable. Exits 0 regardless — it reports the
environment, it does not gate on it.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for doctor


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to a YAML config file (default: anpu.yaml in the current directory, if present)

.PP
\fB--data-dir\fP=""
	data directory for the scan-history DB and caches (default: os.UserConfigDir()/anpu; override with the ANPU_HOME environment variable)

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	show per-stage finding and warning counts


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBanpu(1)\fP


